2. The original Stata 'slopepower' command and example datasets
------------------------------------------------------------------

This package is a translation of the Stata command 'slopepower', described
in:

  Nash, S., K. E. Morgan, C. Frost, and A. Mulick. 2021. Power and
  sample-size calculations for trials that compare slopes over time:
  Introducing the slopepower command. Stata Journal 21(3): 575-601.
  <doi:10.1177/1536867X211045512>

The command's .ado and .sthlp files, and its bundled example datasets
(the source of this package's slpower1, slpower2, and slpower3 data
objects), were published as supporting files of that Stata Journal article
(article st0647) and are copyrighted by StataCorp LLC. Neither the .ado
file, the .sthlp file, nor the article state a license; the applicable
terms are the Stata Journal's own Terms and Conditions of Use
(https://www.stata-journal.com/terms-of-use/), which state:

  "The contents of the supporting files (programs, datasets, and help
  files) may be copied or reproduced by any means whatsoever, in whole or
  in part, as long as any copy or reproduction includes attribution to
  both (1) the author and (2) the Stata Journal."

This package is reproduced and adapted under that permission. Attribution:

  - Author: Stephen Nash, Katy E. Morgan, Chris Frost, and Amy Mulick,
    "Power and sample-size calculations for trials that compare slopes
    over time: Introducing the slopepower command"
  - Journal: Stata Journal 21(3): 575-601 (2021)

The example datasets (slpower1, slpower2, slpower3) are simulated data
whose generating code is given in the appendix of the above article;
they are reproduced here unchanged in value, with only storage types
converted (see data-raw/make-data.R).
